@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Linked-worktree git linkage — two pointer files overlaid, never rewritten

node "Host checkout" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "<main>/.git\nobjects · refs · config · worktrees/" as COMMON <<db>>
  component "<tree>/.git — a FILE\n'gitdir: <main>/.git/worktrees/<name>'" as DOTGIT <<app>>
  component "worktrees/<name>/gitdir\n'<tree>/.git'" as GITDIR <<app>>
}

node "Container" as CONT <<host>> {
  component "/proveo-git\nbind of the shared .git (rw unless gitMode ro)" as CCOMMON <<app>>
  component "/workspace/input | /app\nthe worktree tree" as CTREE <<app>>
  component "overlay: dotgit\n'gitdir: /proveo-git/worktrees/<name>'" as CDOT <<app>>
  component "overlay: gitdir\n'<containerRoot>/.git'" as CGIT <<app>>
}

component "PrepareWorktreeLinks(root)\nwrites both files under PROVEO_HOME" as PREP <<app>>
component "worktree reported 'prunable'\ngit worktree prune deletes the host registration" as PRUNE <<error>>

DOTGIT ARROW_MAIN COMMON : host path
GITDIR ARROW_MAIN DOTGIT : host path
PREP ARROW_MAIN CDOT
PREP ARROW_MAIN CGIT
CDOT ARROW_MAIN CCOMMON : container path
CGIT ARROW_MAIN CDOT : container path
COMMON ARROW_MAIN CCOMMON : bind
CDOT ARROW_ERROR PRUNE : what an incoherent chain causes
CTREE ARROW_OPTIONAL CDOT : nested bind shadows the host file

note right of PREP
  **A linked worktree's ""\.git"" is a FILE, not a directory**, holding
  ""gitdir: <main>/\.git/worktrees/<name>"" — a //host// path that does not
  exist inside the container. Binding the shared ""\.git"" at ""/proveo-git""
  makes objects and refs writable, but leaves the linkage incoherent,
  because two pointer files still disagree with container reality:
  the tree's ""\.git"", and ""worktrees/<name>/gitdir"" pointing back at it.

  **The overlay replaces exactly those two files** with container-correct
  copies, as nested read-only binds — the same shadowing trick
  ""maskEnvMounts"" uses for ""\.env"". The host copies are never rewritten,
  so the operator's own use of the worktree keeps working; only the
  container sees the rewritten chain. ""commondir"" needs no overlay: it is
  already relative (""\.\./\.\."").

  The files are read-only on purpose. Git writes to the per-worktree admin
  dir, never to these pointers — the only writer would be
  ""git worktree move/repair"", which must not reach the host.
end note

note bottom of PRUNE
  **An incoherent chain is not merely cosmetic — it is destructive.**
  ""gitdir"" names a path that is absent in the container, so git marks the
  worktree prunable and ""git worktree prune"" (also reached through ""gc"")
  **deletes** ""<main>/\.git/worktrees/<name>"" on the **host**. The operator's
  worktree is then dead: ""fatal: not a git repository"".

  With the overlay in place ""prune"" is a no-op and the admin dir survives.
end note

note left of CTREE
  **Why the overlay and not ""GIT_DIR""/""GIT_WORK_TREE"".** Env pinning also
  makes commits work, but it is a pin, not a fix, and it fails two ways:

  * a tool that does its own discovery instead of inheriting the env dies
    on the stale path — ""fatal: not a git repository""
  * ""GIT_DIR"" is absolute and process-global, so it captures **any** nested
    or sibling repo the agent visits: ""git -C /other rev-parse --git-dir""
    answers with the outer worktree's admin dir

  A coherent chain needs no pin, so plain discovery works everywhere.
  ""WorktreeEnv"" is kept only as the fallback for when the pointer files
  cannot be written, and the two are never set together.
end note

note bottom of CCOMMON
  **""gitMode: ro"" applies here too.** ""gitOverride"" bails on a worktree —
  it requires ""\.git"" to be a //directory// — so before this the shared
  ""\.git"" was writable no matter what ""gitMode"" said. The read-only state
  now rides on the ""/proveo-git"" bind itself.

  The pointer dir is keyed by //common dir + name//, not name alone: every
  checkout may hold a worktree called 'feature', and a name-only key would
  let one repo's overlay overwrite another's.
end note

' --- IGNORE: layout hints (do not edit) ---
HOST -down[hidden]- PREP
' --- END IGNORE ---
@enduml
